# env file
.env

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/

.cursor/
test_data/

# Agent tooling. Kept here rather than in .git/info/exclude, which is local to
# one clone and which the sdist build does not read — so an exclude-only entry
# shipped .claude/settings.local.json inside the release artifact.
.claude/

# Working notes that are not part of the public repo. Here for the same reason
# .claude/ is: hatchling builds the sdist from .gitignore, so these three spent
# a release cycle in .git/info/exclude — absent from GitHub, present in the
# tarball. docs/prompt-analysis.md quotes a real assembled prompt, opponent
# handles and all, which is the one thing this project promises not to disclose.
docs/opensource-readiness/03-code-audit.md
docs/feature-ideas.md
docs/prompt-analysis.md

# Corpus-derived goldens. Frozen at the Python cutover: the Go capture tool
# they came from is gone, so these cannot be regenerated — see
# testdata/golden/MANIFEST.md. They embed real opponent usernames (P0-8).
testdata/golden/summaries.json
testdata/golden/analysis.json
testdata/golden/prompts/

